  "query_preview": "/WEDNESDAY NIGHT THROUGH MONDAY/...\nIssued at 258 PM CDT Tue Oct 13 2026\n\nTheta-e advection increases later Wednesday afternoon into\nevening ahead of the upper low coming out of the Four Corners\narea Wednesday, crossing through the Central Plains Thursday and\nthen being absorbed by the strong upper trough coming out of \nCanada and swinging through the region Thursday night into\nFriday. After being shunted to the south during a good portion\nof the daytime Wednesday, moisture returns late Wednesday night\nthrough Thursday. The end result is any showery activity\nWednesday evening becomes more widespread rain during the day\nThursday with conditions drying out Thursday evening. Windy and\nmuch cooler conditions will follow Thursday night into Friday as\nlows drop into the upper 30s to 40s with highs Friday in the\n50s. Temperatures drop further Friday night into Saturday with\nlows in the low 30s introducing the possibility for some frost\nto start the weekend. The windy conditions from the daytime will\nsubside by evening as a high pressure moves into the area. This\nhigh and an upper ridge overhead will keep conditions dry for\nFriday through the weekend.",
